            "summary": "ADVANCED, NOT CLOSED, by pic-e (run 0095). Owner released. Scheme.DivFamily HAS AN INHABITANT; the seam sorry fgaPicardRepresentability is untouched and NO antecedent of it is witnessed for any curve.\n\nLANDED, DO NOT REDO. Picard/DivFamilyZero.lean + Picard/DivFamilyZeroAbel.lean, both rooted at AlgebraicJacobian.lean. 34 declarations across the two files, ZERO code sorries, ALL 34 axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] against fgaPicardRepresentability firing sorryAx in the same probe with oleans rebuilt FIRST. Verified independently by a fresh-context audit which found four defects, all accepted and fixed (see below).\n\n* DivFamily.zero pi T -- the EMPTY DIVISOR, for ARBITRARY pi : X -> S and T : Over S. F = 0, q = 0, so ker q = O_{X_T} and the divisor condition holds because O/O = 0 cuts out D = empty. No hypothesis on pi: not proper, not smooth, not separated. THE FIRST INHABITANT: at the parent commit, 148 mentions of DivFamily in AJC and zero producers (audited independently; both numbers exactly confirmed).\n* WHY IT IS NOT VACUOUS, measured not asserted: IsLocallyTrivial (0 : Y.Modules) is FALSE at every point (restrict-of-zero is zero, forcing subsingleton sections, contra Scheme.component_nontrivial). So kerLocallyTrivial at F = 0 asserts a rank-ONE statement and genuinely excludes the rival 'unit divisor' F = O, q = id.\n* Base change: pullbackAlong_zero, so DivFunctor.map_zeroClass makes zeroClass a GLOBAL SECTION of Div, not a per-object choice. fiberDeg_zero / hasFiberDeg_zero give degree 0 everywhere, hence an inhabitant of (DivFunctorDeg pi 0).obj T.\n* PicScheme.abelMap_zero: A([empty]) = 0, Kleiman's O(empty) = O normalisation and the FIRST COMPUTED VALUE of abelMap in the project (audited: no prior declaration evaluates abelMap/abelDeg/abelMapWitness at a closed term). abelDeg_zero is the same through the degree-refined map. Stated at abelMapWitness's instance with no [HasAbelMap C] binder, so the trivial constant-zero inhabitant cannot satisfy it.\n* REUSABLE BRICKS ABSENT FROM MATHLIB (audited against mathlib + both projects): Modules.isFinitePresentation_of_isZero (a zero sheaf of modules is finitely presented -- not synthesizable), Modules.coversTop_singleton_top, Modules.preservesZeroMorphisms_overFunctor (proved; instance search fails at 1.6M heartbeats), Modules.isZero_free_pempty.\n\nWHAT IS STILL OPEN, and it is the row's remaining content. Div^0 is NOT represented by the terminal object: this file proves the Nonempty half only. The missing half is Subsingleton ((DivFunctorDeg pi 0).obj T) -- that the empty divisor is the ONLY degree-0 one. AUDIT-CONFIRMED that Nonempty + Subsingleton at every T SUFFICES, with naturality free (homEquiv_comp closes by Subsingleton.elim). So this row is one Subsingleton away from a genuine RepresentableBy producer on the divisor side.\n\nDO NOT re-derive it from the sibling. AJCR has the analogous Subsingleton landed (instSubsingletonDivFamZarZero, and the general-ring form with a full RepresentableBy producer). It does NOT transport, and the reason is sharper than the carrier mismatch: their proof never passes through a finrank -- it runs on IsCertified and rankAtStalk over Away localisations of section rings. AJC's fiberDeg IS a Module.finrank of fibre sections. Their success is also evidence against pricing this as a finiteness question at all.\n\nNOT DISCHARGED, stated because it is the natural over-reading: PicScheme.classDegree_ne_zero_of_exists_pos_fiberDeg (Picard/IdentityComponent.lean) needs a family of degree d != 0. The empty divisor has degree 0, so it is precisely the family that acceptance test cannot use. That producer needs a rational point and the positivity bridge pic-b is building.\n\nFOUR AUDIT FINDINGS AGAINST MY OWN WORK, all accepted: (1) Module.Flat.of_subsingleton' was REDUNDANT -- mathlib's Module.Free.of_subsingleton is a priority-100 instance so the goal closes by inferInstance; my evidence had been an exact? failure, which does not run instance synthesis. Deleted. (2) Three citations named the FILE not the NAMESPACE and all three failed #check; fixed, and all 13 cited names are now #check-verified. (3) 'properSupport is a real hypothesis for a nonempty divisor' was never measured; dropped. (4) 'no lane holds the Subsingleton' was FALSE.",
